    "body_text": "Skip to content Buy Rent House Prices Find Agent Commercial Inspire Overseas Sign in Sign in Buy Property for sale New homes for sale Property valuation Investors Mortgages Rent Property to rent Student property to rent Find Agent Find estate agents House prices Sold house prices Instant online valuation Commercial Commercial property to rent Commercial property for sale Advertise Inspire Moving stories Property news Energy efficiency Property guides Housing trends Overseas blog Mortgage guides Overseas All countries Spain France Portugal Italy Greece Currency Sell Overseas property See similar properties Property photo 1 of 20. 1/20 Erskine Road, London, E17 £1,500 pcm £346 pw Tenancy info Added today Letting details Let available date: 01/06/2026 Deposit: £1,730 Furnish type: Unfurnished Council Tax: Ask agent PROPERTY TYPE Flat BEDROOMS 1 BATHROOMS 1 SIZE Ask agent 1 +14 Key features One bedroom warehouse conversionPopular locationWalthamstow Central locationBright and spacious accommodationMust be seenAvailable October 2019 Description Set within a charming warehouse conversion, formerly a historic button factory, this fantastic one bedroom apartment offers a unique blend of character, space and modern living in the heart of Walthamstow Central. The property benefits from a bright and spacious reception room with plenty of natural light, creating an ideal living and entertaining space for tenants. The modern fitted kitchen offers ample storage and worktop space, whilst the well-proportioned double bedroom provides comfortable accommodation. Completing the property is a contemporary bathroom finished to a good standard. Ideally positioned for renters seeking both convenience and lifestyle, the apartment is just moments from Walthamstow Central Station, providing excellent transport links via the Victoria Line and London Overground with direct access into Central London, Oxford Circus, King’s Cross and Liverpool Street. Numerous bus routes are also nearby, making commuting simple and efficient. The property is surrounded by a wide range of local amenities including the famous Walthamstow Market, Europe’s longest outdoor market, alongside an excellent selection of independent cafés, restaurants, bars and shops. Nearby shopping options also include The Mall Walthamstow, local supermarkets and a variety of fitness facilities including PureGym and The Gym Group. For tenants who enjoy outdoor space and a more active lifestyle, the apartment is ideally located close to several well-known green spaces. Lloyd Park, located approximately 0.8 miles away, offers landscaped gardens, tennis courts, an outdoor gym and the popular William Morris Gallery. Walthamstow Wetlands, one of Europe’s largest urban wetland reserves, is also within easy reach and provides beautiful walking and cycling routes, wildlife areas and waterside scenery. Additionally, the open green spaces of Hollow Ponds and Epping Forest are nearby, perfect for weekend walks, running routes and outdoor activities. This property would make an excellent home for professional tenants or couples looking for a stylish and well-connected apartment in one of East London’s most vibrant and sought-after rental locations. A licence restricts number of tenants to a maximum of 2 unrelated persons or a family EPC Rating: D. Council Tax Band: B. Rent excludes utilities, the tenancy deposit and any other permitted payments. Monthly rent is £1,500.00 PCM Deposit payable is £1,730.76 based on the advertised rent A Holding Deposit of £346.15, based on the advertised rent, is required to reserve this property. Min Term 1 year fixed term. Broadband type availability & speed: / Mobile coverage checker: Parking permit availability from local authority: / Additional parking info: Please note this is a car free development and therefore on street or off-street parking permits are not available. Please contact us for further information or visit our website Read full description 